; NextDAAD sampled-SFX DI-exposure ear fixture (2026-08-03).
;
; Compiled by tests\build-tests.ps1 on every run; staged as the active
; sd\GAME.DDB by tests\build-tests.ps1 -SfxDi, which also generates the
; two stimulus tones with tests\audio\mktone.py and stages them as
; sd\001.WAV (16 kHz) and sd\002.WAV (20 kHz).
;
; RUN SHEET: .superpowers\sdd\sfx-di-audible-test.md. Read it before
; running - one leg of this test is MODE-SENSITIVE and gives a false
; negative on VGA4/VGA5/VGA6.
;
; WHAT IT MAKES AUDIBLE
; overlay2's dma_copy programmed and ran each picture-copy chunk inside
; one DI bracket. Before 4cda75e that bracket was 1904 T, longer than
; the sampled-SFX CTC period at every rate at or above ~14.2 kHz - so a
; graphics copy running under a playing sample SUPPRESSED CTC ticks.
; Nothing is dropped, clicked or truncated: ctc_isr simply does not run,
; the DAC holds its previous byte one extra period, and the effect plays
; LONG AND FLAT. The only observable is PITCH.
;
; WHY GFX 0 0 AND NOT A LOCATION PICTURE. The mechanism is duty-cycle
; limited: what matters is the fraction of wall time spent inside DI
; brackets. A DISPLAY 0 location blit is only 21% in-DI (its 62 ms is
; dominated by gfx_row_fetch's LDIR staging), which at the shipped
; 16 kHz on HDMI is 2.47% slow for 62 ms - 43 cents, at or below the
; percept threshold, and an ear cannot certify it. GFX 0/1 runs the same
; dma_copy back to back with almost nothing between the brackets: 78%
; in-DI, 9.14% slow, and it can be repeated without limit. Same defect,
; same code path, roughly 4x the amplitude - a steady 440 Hz tone drops
; to 399.8 Hz (1.66 semitones) the instant the burst starts and snaps
; back when it stops.
;
; l2Mode is 0 (256x192) here and stays 0: nothing in this fixture loads
; a picture or a video, and those are the only things that call
; l2_mode_set. So each GFX 0 0 is 384 dma_copy calls / 34.8 ms on HDMI
; before the fix and 44.5 ms after it. Staging a 320-wide title or
; picture alongside this fixture would make the surface 320x256 and
; every GFX 0 0 640 calls instead - the PITCH is unchanged (the duty
; cycle is the same 78%), only the burst gets longer. Stage nothing else.
;
; NO MUSIC. The AKY player holds interrupts off ~5500 T every frame
; while a song plays, which costs the sample engine a CONTINUOUS ~0.67%
; at 16 kHz - a standing pitch error that would sit under both phases
; and blunt the comparison. -SfxDi stale-cleans sd\*.AKY and stages
; none, so nothing autoplays and the reference phases are clean.
;
; THE TONE. tests\audio\mktone.py: 48000 bytes (exactly the 48K reserved
; audio floor, banks 25-27, so the load cannot fail on pool pressure),
; 8-bit unsigned mono, full-scale 440 Hz, centred on 128 = DAC_SILENCE,
; a whole number of cycles end to end (1320 at 16 kHz, 1056 at 20 kHz).
; Played with SFX n 2 = LOOPED: aud_smp_copy rewinds the source mid-copy
; and the ring never sees the seam, so the tone runs continuously for as
; long as the leg needs and there is no run-out to mistake for a result.
; A missing WAV is a documented silent no-op (h_sfx falls through to the
; AY-effect path, and no GAME.SFB is staged) - so if you hear nothing at
; all, that is a STAGING miss, not an audio result.
;
; SEQUENCE (T16 and T20 share it; T16 also runs once automatically at
; boot, so the readout needs no typing):
;   1/3  0.76 s of clean reference tone, no graphics
;   2/3  40 back-to-back GFX 0 0 surface copies
;   3/3  0.76 s of clean reference tone again, then stop
; The burst TAKES LONGER after the fix (~1.4 s -> ~1.8 s). That is the
; ruled-for cost, not a symptom. The pitch is the readout, not the
; duration.
;
; PAUSE IS SCALED BY DRC. drb.php multiplies every PAUSE by
; getBaseLength/DEFAULT_NOTE_DURAION = 120/200 = 0.6 for the ZX NEXT
; target, so the authored PAUSE 63 reaches the interpreter as 38 frames
; = 0.76 s at 50 Hz. Do not "correct" 63 to 38 here or the reference
; phases halve. build-tests.ps1 asserts the compiled byte.

; System flags used by name (DAAD BLANK template spellings)
#define fPlayer             38
#define fDarkF              28

/CTL
_
/VOC
NORTH  2  noun
SOUTH  3  noun
LOOK   4  verb
T16    60 verb
T20    61 verb
HUSH   62 verb
/STX
/0  "It's too dark to see anything."
/1  "I can also see:"
/2  "What now?"
/3  "What next?"
/4  "What should I do now?"
/5  "What should I do next?"
/6  "I didn't understand."
/7  "I can't go in that direction."
/8  "I can't do that."
/9  "I have with me:"
/10 "I am wearing:"
/11 " "
/12 "Are you sure?"
/13 "Another go?"
/14 " "
/15 "OK."
/16 "Press any key."
/17 " "
/18 " "
/19 " "
/20 " "
/21 " "
/22 " "
/23 "I'm not wearing one of those."
/24 "I can't. My hands are full."
/25 "I already have the _."
/26 "There isn't one of those here."
/27 "I can't carry any more things."
/28 "I don't have one of those."
/29 "I'm already wearing the _."
/30 "Y"
/31 "N"
/32 "More..."
/33 ">"
/34 " "
/35 " "
/36 "I now have the _."
/37 "I'm now wearing the _."
/38 "I've removed the _."
/39 "I've dropped the _."
/40 "I can't wear the _."
/41 "I can't remove the _."
/42 "I can't remove the _. My hands are full."
/43 "The _ weighs too much for me."
/44 "The _ is in the"
/45 "The _ isn't in the"
/46 ", "
/47 " and "
/48 ".#n"
/49 "I don't have the _."
/50 "I'm not wearing the _."
/51 "."
/52 "There isn't one of those in the"
/53 "Nothing."
/54 " "
/55 " "
/56 " "
/57 "I/O Error"
/58 " "
/59 "File name error."
/60 "Type in name of file."
/MTX
/0 "NEXTDAAD SAMPLED-SFX DI EXPOSURE - EAR FIXTURE#n"
/OTX
/0 "a brass lamp"
/LTX
/0 ""
/1 "The listening room."
/CON
/0
NORTH 1
/1
SOUTH 0
/OBJ
/0    1   1   _ _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _   _ _
/PRO 0
> _ _   AT 0
        PROCESS 6
> _ _   WINDOW 1
        WINAT 0 0
        WINSIZE 25 127
        CLEAR fDarkF
> _ _   WINDOW 1
        DESC @fPlayer
> _ _   PROCESS 1
/PRO 1
> _ _   PARSE 0
        REDO
> _ _   PROCESS 5
        ISDONE
        REDO
> _ _   MOVE fPlayer
        CLS
        RESTART
> _ _   SYSMESS 8
        REDO
/PRO 5
; ---- the shipped-rate leg (001.WAV, 16000 Hz) ----
; GFX 0 6 clears the BACK surface to transparent first, so the 40
; copies below move a known-clean surface onto the front and the text
; stays readable. It is setup, not stimulus - it runs before the tone
; starts.
> T16 _   MES "#nLEG 16 kHz - 001.WAV, the rate everything ships#n"
          GFX 0 6
          SFX 1 2
          PROCESS 7
          DONE
; ---- the published-ceiling leg (002.WAV, 20000 Hz) ----
; 20000 Hz is AUD_RATE_MAX - what README.md and authoring-kit\SETUP.md
; publish as supported and what a DAAD-DOS SOUNDS set drops in at. It
; is NOT a rate anything in this project ships, so this leg exercises
; the documented surface, not the shipped one. Predicted drop is 2.7x
; the 16 kHz leg's.
> T20 _   MES "#nLEG 20 kHz - 002.WAV, README's published maximum#n"
          GFX 0 6
          SFX 2 2
          PROCESS 7
          DONE
; ---- panic stop ----
> HUSH _  MES "#ntone stopped#n"
          SFX 0 5
          DONE
/PRO 7
; The three phases. Each MES lands immediately before the phase it
; names, so the phase-2 line marks the pitch-drop onset and the phase-3
; line marks the snap-back.
> _ _   MES "1/3 REFERENCE - steady 440 Hz, no graphics#n"
        PAUSE 63
> _ _   MES "2/3 BURST - 40 x GFX 0 0 surface copies#n"
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
        GFX 0 0
> _ _   MES "3/3 REFERENCE - steady 440 Hz again#n"
        PAUSE 63
        SFX 0 5
        MES "leg done#n"
/PRO 6
> _ _   WINDOW 1
        WINAT 0 0
        WINSIZE 25 127
        PAPER 0
        INK 7
        CLS
        MESSAGE 0
> _ _   MES "A steady 440 Hz tone, then 40 GFX 0 0 surface#n"
        MES "copies, then the tone again. Listen for PITCH,#n"
        MES "not for duration - the burst is MEANT to take#n"
        MES "longer on the fixed build.#n#n"
        MES "T16   16 kHz leg (001.WAV) - the shipped rate#n"
        MES "T20   20 kHz leg (002.WAV) - README's maximum#n"
        MES "HUSH  stop the tone#n#n"
        MES "Run sheet: sfx-di-audible-test.md#n"
; The 16 kHz leg runs once here, at boot, so the readout needs no
; typing at all. Same four condacts as T16 in /PRO 5 - the verb table
; cannot be reused for this because no verb has been parsed yet.
> _ _   MES "#nAUTO-RUN: 16 kHz leg#n"
        GFX 0 6
        SFX 1 2
        PROCESS 7
        GOTO 1
/END
